/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (Across Ireland, change is beginning. Local councils have introduced free period products in public buildings such as libraries and community centres. Schools and colleges are increasingly recognised as key spaces where dignity and access must be guaranteed, not optional.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (This is not a problem limited to one community or income group. Menstrual poverty affects girls from low-income households, those living in temporary accommodation, and young people whose families are already under financial pressure. For many, the challenge is not knowing where to turn when help is needed.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (Providing free products is about more than supply. It is about sending a message. Menstruation is normal. Support is available. No one should be excluded from education or opportunity because of their period.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
