/Title (Period poverty in Ireland is not a distant or isolated issue. Research and reports show that nearly 50 percent of girls have experienced some form of menstrual poverty. This includes struggling to afford period products, missing school days, or using unsuitable alternatives because there is no other choice. In practical terms, this means that in almost every classroom, there are girls quietly carrying a burden they should never have to bear.)
