/Title (For some girls, period poverty looks like staying home from school when their period arrives. For others, it means avoiding sports, school trips, or social activities. Over time, these interruptions affect confidence, participation, and academic engagement. What begins as a monthly challenge can grow into a long-term barrier.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 408 0 R
/Prev 561 0 R
/Next 687 0 R
>>
endobj
687 0 obj
<<
/Title (ANUA starts by naming this reality honestly. Period poverty is not about personal failure. It is about access, dignity, and equality. If girls are expected to show up, learn, and succeed, then managing their period safely must be treated as a basic educational need, not an afterthought.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 408 0 R
/Prev 686 0 R
/Next 562 0 R
>>
