/Title (Student Caoimhe Dowling spoke about how this struggle continued into college. Buying period products became a source of stress, with essential items competing against food and transport when money was tight. Others, like student advocate Sheenagh Rowland, recall school days when friends had no option but to use tissue, managing their periods in silence and embarrassment.)
